  "isDnd":false,
  "layers":[
    {"$GMRAssetLayer":"","%Name":"Instructions","assets":[
        {"$GMRSpriteGraphic":"v1","%Name":"graphic_49EC7C24","animationSpeed":1.0,"colour":4294967295,"frozen":false,"headPosition":0.0,"ignore":false,"inheritedItemId":null,"inheritItemSettings":false,"name":"graphic_49EC7C24","resourceType":"GMRSpriteGraphic","resourceVersion":"2.0","rotation":0.0,"scaleX":64.0,"scaleY":36.0,"spriteId":{"name":"spr_InfoOverlay","path":"sprites/spr_InfoOverlay/spr_InfoOverlay.yy",},"x":0.0,"y":0.0,},
        {"$GMRTextItem":"v3","%Name":"text_539FE0DE","alignment":0,"charSpacing":0.0,"colour":4294967295,"fontId":{"name":"fnt_Info","path":"fonts/fnt_Info/fnt_Info.yy",},"frameH":680.0,"frameW":1240.0,"frozen":false,"ignore":false,"inheritedItemId":null,"inheritItemSettings":false,"lineSpacing":5.0,"name":"text_539FE0DE","paragraphSpacing":0.0,"resourceType":"GMRTextItem","resourceVersion":"2.0","rotation":0.0,"scaleX":1.0,"scaleY":1.0,"text":"This demonstration showcases the CIMPLI events, logging and workers functionality.\r\n\r\nEvents can be used for separating state checks and handling.\r\nFor example, a text box may send an event every time its content changes, and then one or more components may respond to these changes (or none at all).\r\n\r\nLogging is mostly used for keeping track of important occurrences for diagnostics purposes.\r\n\r\nWorkers can be used for performing long-running tasks over multiple steps.\r\n\r\n***\r\n\r\nThe demonstration contains a sum calculation service, allowing the user to calculate the sum from 1 to 20k, from 1 to 60k and from 1 to 100k. The terms are summed individually over multiple frames, and the Worker system manages the long-running process without blocking the game.\r\n\r\nThe system keeps track of various events related to the task processing and changing state.\r\nYou can add or remove observers for each of these events; you can even add multiple observers for the same event.\r\nWhen an event happens, each of its observers will log a relevant message at a specific logging level.\r\n\r\nYou can also change the threshold of logging level, from least important TRACE to most severe CRITICAL level.\r\nOnly messages with the level matching or exceeding the threshold importance will be logged. It doesn't affect already logged messages.","wrap":true,"x":20.0,"y":80.0,},
        {"$GMRTextItem":"v3","%Name":"text_555154E3","alignment":0,"charSpacing":0.0,"colour":4292149119,"fontId":{"name":"fnt_Title","path":"fonts/fnt_Title/fnt_Title.yy",},"frameH":40.0,"frameW":800.0,"frozen":false,"ignore":false,"inheritedItemId":null,"inheritItemSettings":false,"lineSpacing":5.0,"name":"text_555154E3","paragraphSpacing":0.0,"resourceType":"GMRTextItem","resourceVersion":"2.0","rotation":0.0,"scaleX":1.0,"scaleY":1.0,"text":"COUNTER OBSERVER DEMO","wrap":true,"x":20.0,"y":20.0,},
      ],"depth":0,"effectEnabled":true,"effectType":null,"gridX":20,"gridY":20,"hierarchyFrozen":false,"inheritLayerDepth":false,"inheritLayerSettings":false,"inheritSubLayers":true,"inheritVisibility":true,"layers":[],"name":"Instructions","properties":[],"resourceType":"GMRAssetLayer","resourceVersion":"2.0","userdefinedDepth":false,"visible":false,},
